# fisher-38w, 2026-11-27. Staged for fisher-38w before the engine changes.
# Stockfish 19 (sf_19, edb0d9d), Homebrew arm64 bottle at /opt/homebrew/bin/stockfish,
# probed 2026-11-27. OptionsMap::setoption consumes the token in the name
# position whatever it is, then reads the option name up to the token value.
# https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish/blob/edb0d9db6731067ec50ce619ff372b463bc4dd5d/src/ucioption.cpp#L43-L60
# Owner decision on fisher-38w (2026-11-27): follow Stockfish 19.
# See README.md for each probe input and its output.
# Searched info spelling and the depth-1 scores: as multipv/settings.uci
# (fisher-r6y D41, D12, D13, fisher-8hc answers 5 and 6). Every depth-1 score
# from startpos is cp 0 by material (fisher-2aj rules 2 and 3).

# Stockfish 19: send the bytes 73 65 74 6f 70 74 69 6f 6e 20 c2 a0 6e 61 6d 65
# 20 4d 75 6c 74 69 50 56 20 76 61 6c 75 65 20 32 0a. U+00A0 is not a
# separator (whitespace/README.md), so the token in the name position is
# "<U+00A0>name", not name. Stockfish consumes it and sets MultiPV to 2.
> setoption \xc2\xa0name MultiPV value 2
# Stockfish 19 printed nothing before readyok, so fisher must stay silent
# here: one readyok and nothing else.
> isready
< readyok
> position startpos
# Stockfish 19 answered go depth 1 with multipv 1 and multipv 2, so MultiPV
# is 2. fisher reports one searched info line per variation (D12, D13); a
# setting above 1 uses {nodes} (expectations/README.md, MultiPV).
> go depth 1
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 1 multipv 2 score cp 0 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}
> quit
! exit
